{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And rested.</b> As the Targum renders: וְנָח — and every expression of נֹפֶשׁ is an expression of נֶפֶשׁ, that He restores His soul and breath upon resting from the exertion of the work. And of Him concerning whom it is written ״לֹא יִיעַף וְלֹא יִיגָע״ (Isaiah 40), and all His action is by utterance — did Scripture write 'rest' concerning Him? Only to give relief to the ear, what it is able to hear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:00.370351961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}